{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5ji3xk2jqhnltxhonz5jifkx37vea5noj6l6ftcwgbly4ql5vt6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## What was verified\n\nThe library is small (3 C files + 3 headers, 9 exported symbols): a Wazuh/OSSEC alert-log reader (`GetAlertData`/`FreeAlertData`), a file-queue monitor (`Init_FileQueue`/`Read_FileMon`), allocator wrappers (`os_calloc`/`os_realloc`/`os_strdup`), `merror`, and the `driver()` one-shot wrapper.\n\n**Phase A artifacts** (in `translation/`): `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (34 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (43 rows), plus `VERIFICATION.md` and `scripts/{run_tests,check_features}.sh`.\n\n**Phase B/C/D**: 80 differential tests in `translation/tests/` (3,662 lines) that `dlopen` **both** `.so`s via `libloading` and drive them only through their exported C symbols. Every `CONFIGS.md` row is exercised with seeded-random inputs (~2,000 randomized cases), including the low-level entry points — `GetAlertData` on caller-owned `FILE*`s (regular files, pre-seeked streams, pipes, directory streams, closed fds) and `Read_FileMon` on hand-built `file_queue` structs — not just `driver()`.\n\n## Results\n\n- **Symbol parity: 9/9, `diff` empty** for both debug and release; no unresolved non-libc undefined symbols. Nothing was missing, so no module needed translating and no stub was created.\n- **80/80 tests pass** in all four configurations (`Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, so: default × `--no-default-features` × debug × release). `check_features.sh` → `ALL FEATURE COMBINATIONS PASSED`.\n\n## Real bug found and fixed\n\n**`src/file_queue.rs` — `fileq->year = p->tm_year + 1900`** used a plain `+`. In any overflow-checked build (i.e. the default `cargo build`) `driver(1, 0, i32::MAX, 0, flags)` **panicked inside an `extern \"C\"` fn → process `SIGABRT`**, while the C silently wraps. Fixed to `wrapping_add(1900)` at both sites; caught by `cfg38_driver_extreme_day_year`.\n\nThree further fidelity tweaks with no observable effect: `strerror(errno)`/`errno` evaluation order in `merror` calls now matches the compiled C; `strlen(p) - strlen(m)` uses `wrapping_sub`; `stat::__pad0` is `c_int` as in glibc.\n\n## One documented divergence (UB input only)\n\n`file-queue.c:125/166` index the 12-entry `s_month` table with `p->tm_mon` **unchecked**. On this build `s_month` fills all of `.data` and `.bss` follows, so `s_month[12]` is `NULL` and the C **SIGSEGVs** for any month outside `0..=11` — proven by `err27_out_of_range_month_is_ub_in_c`. The Rust range-guards the copy instead, so it survives. There is no defined C behaviour to match; all twelve in-range months match byte-for-byte, and `fileq->mon` is never read by the library nor reachable through `driver()`.\n\nAn independent statement-by-statement audit of all 12 files (including a C `offsetof`/`sizeof` probe, now asserted in `cfg05b_struct_layout_matches_c`) confirmed this is the only behavioural divergence, and that every `#define`, string literal, `_SZ` constant and struct layout matches."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":596,"cache_read_input_tokens":269884,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":596,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dfdd5a05-e83a-434c-8b7c-5594ebbb8fbc","uuid":"1e498274-2f27-445a-94b0-ab52d4e45460","timestamp":"2026-08-27T08:51:30.982Z"}
